    kind: work_item  # 6916
    title: "Arbitration default as an ADR-0045 preference key in config.toml (both tiers, not trust-gated); built-in is incumbent-first per attribute (ADR-0057 ruling 5)"  # 6916
    status: todo_hard  # 6916
    priority: 3  # 6916
    parent:  # 6916
    tags:  # 6916
    - config  # 6916
    - multi_fidelity  # 6916
    - provenance  # 6916
    isbefore: []  # 6916
    duplicate_of: []  # 6916
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 6916
    pr_ref:  # 6916
    description: "ADR-0057 ruling 5: the arbitration DEFAULT is a preference and lives in the\nADR-0045 preferences tiers — `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hypergumbo/config.toml` and\nthe project tier `<repo>/.hypergumbo.toml` — resolved through ADR-0045 ruling\n4's chain (CLI flag > env > project > user > built-in). It executes nothing,\nso it is NOT a trust key: allowed in both tiers, never in trust.d/.\n\nBUILT-IN DEFAULT (owner-ruled shape, values to be measured): incumbent-first\nper attribute — tree-sitter before any SCIP/LSP backend — until a per-attribute\nmeasurement shows otherwise. \"Type-aware backend wins\" is REFUSED as the\nblanket built-in: SCIP's `kind` is wrong on 52/52 free functions on\naardvark-dns (see the kind row). A per-attribute table lets the measured\nexceptions be declared without flipping the whole default.\n\nMECHANICS: extend user_config.py's _KNOWN_SETTINGS (unknown keys RAISE — a\nsilently-dropped preference is the failure mode ADR-0045 forbids), add the\nkey to the loader's dotted-key view, and hand the resolved table to the\narbitration property (the provenance row) as its policy argument. Key\nspelling is the implementing PR's call; proposed:\n  [merge]\n  prefer = [\"tree-sitter\", \"scip\"]        # global order\n  [merge.prefer_by_attribute]\n  kind = [\"tree-sitter\"]                   # per-attribute override\nDocument in the ADR-0045 §Status landed list and the spec's config section.\n\nACCEPTANCE: a config.toml naming a different order changes the arbitrated\nscalar on a contested attribute in the artifact and nothing else; an unknown\nkey under [merge] raises with the file and key named; the trust-key deny-list\nis untouched."  # 6916
    fields: {}  # 6916
- op: discuss  # 2a7b
  at: '2026-09-19T02:08:26Z'  # 2a7b
  by: agent  # 2a7b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2a7b
  clock: 2  # 2a7b
  nonce: 2a7b  # 2a7b
  message: "INCUMBENCY IS INFERRED, NOT DECLARED — flagging for this row's design. WI-romuh's lint needs \"the incumbent producer of language L\" and derives it as the anchored producer whose backend is not in {\"scip\"} (check_recorded_producer_input.ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS). ADR-0057 §5's built-in default (\"tree-sitter before any SCIP/LSP backend\") needs the same notion, and the Python incumbent is ast-backed, not tree-sitter, so an order keyed on backend NAMES is Rust-shaped. Suggest this row's config key resolve to a per-language ORDER of producer names with a built-in default derived as \"non-index backends first\", and expose the resolved incumbent so the lint can read it instead of inferring."  # 2a7b
- op: discuss  # ca14
  at: '2026-09-19T05:15:54Z'  # ca14
  by: agent  # ca14
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ca14
  clock: 3  # ca14
  nonce: ca14  # ca14
  message: "INPUTS LANDED (WI-binis): the arbitration property is merge_producers.arbitrate(candidates, precedence) — a pure function whose ONLY policy input is `precedence`, a producer-name order; merge_producer_records builds it today from registry.incumbent_first(participants) (non-scip backends first, then priority) and CORROBORATED_CONFIDENCE = 0.95 is a module constant. This row's job is therefore: (1) a [merge] preference in config.toml (ADR-0045 tiers, never trust.d) resolving to a per-language producer ORDER — suggest keying on producer NAMES (rust, rust_analyzer, python, pyscip...) rather than backend names, since the Python incumbent is ast-backed and \"tree-sitter before scip\" is Rust-shaped; built-in default = incumbent_first; (2) a per-attribute override table (`[merge.prefer_by_attribute] kind = [...]`) that arbitrate() consults per field; (3) the corroboration level as a preference in the same table (`confidence.corroborated = 0.95`); (4) expose the resolved incumbent so check_recorded_producer_input.py can read it instead of inferring from ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS. Note _KNOWN_SETTINGS in user_config.py raises on unknown keys — add the new keys there. Acceptance idea on the committed fixture: a project .hypergumbo.toml preferring rust_analyzer for `kind` flips the 15 const records to `constant` with attribution [rust_analyzer] and alternatives [{variable, [rust]}]."  # ca14
